    "body": "Yes, the problem is that you don't know if the document you bind to is\ngoing to be replaced with a different one. I'll see if I can get an example\ntogether soon.\n\nThis wouldn't necessarily only fire for cross-origin iframes, but it\nwouldn't be as useful in that situation.\n\nOn Fri, 9 Dec 2016, 18:15 Domenic Denicola, <notifications@github.com>\nwrote:\n\n> Can you explain what the problem is with\n> iframe.contentDocument.onreadystatechange and\n> iframe.contentDocument.readyState?\n>\n> I don't think we generally want to introduce APIs that only work for\n> same-origin iframes on HTMLIFrameElement.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2161#issuecomment-266082762>, or mute\n> the thread\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/ABvdEzuoFHD4MYiZ3BvBcKAUB2n7eHj6ks5rGZq-gaJpZM4LJCQ5>\n> .\n>\n",
