    "updated_at": "2025-04-26T09:53:16Z",
    "body": "I have a similar issue (perhaps same?). What's the expected behaviour, according to the spec, of the following example?\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <title></title>\n\n    <script type=\"module\">\n      const iframe = document.querySelector(\"iframe\")\n      iframe.srcdoc = '<a href=\"go\">link</a>'\n\n      // In Chrome, commenting out the following timeout makes the unload event fire\n      // In Firefox, timeout is not necessary\n      // In Safari on macOS, I couldn't get it to work at all\n\n      // setTimeout(() => {\n        iframe.contentWindow.addEventListener(\"unload\", event => {\n          console.log('onUnload')\n        })\n      // }, 500)\n    </script>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <!--\n      according to this comment https://stackoverflow.com/questions/50480198/#comment91133528_50480492\n      the iframe cannot escape it's sandbox even though we have allow-scripts and allow-same-origin\n      because its on a different origin than the parent.\n      Or is srcdoc treated as same origin?\n      TODO: verify this\n    -->\n    <iframe sandbox=\"allow-modals allow-scripts allow-same-origin\">\n  </body>\n</html>\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
